        id = "midiModeHelp",
        title = "MIDI Mode Help",
        font = "console20",
        align = "Left",
        width = 1200,
        message = "\nMIDI modes:\n\n\nIn ALL modes you need a controller which has endless-rotating encoders!\n\n\nStandard:\n\n---------\n\nThe controler is sending standard relative midi.\n\nThere are 3 standard relative midi modes.\n\nFor example, in mode-2, turn right is 65 (+1), turn left is 63 (-1).\n\nThe faster you turn the encoder, then higher values are sent (aka. Acceleration)\n\n\nAbsolute: (Available ONLY from MA3 version 2.0.x)\n\n---------\n\nThe controler is sending absolute midi values 1-127.\n\nIf the encoder is at 0 and you keep turning left, it keeps sending 0 value.\n\nSame for value of 127 and turning right. (No acceleration).\n\n\nCustom:\n\n-------\n\nThe controler is sending a specific value for turn-left,\n\nand another value for turn-right.\n\n(No acceleration)\n\n\n\n\n "
    })
end
